```"},{"name":"mcp__powershell__cancel","description":"Interrupt the command currently running in the agent's active console. Stops a runaway/long-running PowerShell pipeline (Start-Sleep, a loop, a slow cmdlet) by stopping the running pipeline, AND sends Ctrl+C to break a native CLI that is looping or waiting on stdin (git, npm, ssh, ping, etc.). A command stuck in a non-cooperative blocking call (e.g. [Threading.Thread]::Sleep, a blocking socket/read) may NOT stop — use close_console for that. It also does NOT cancel a PowerShell host prompt (Read-Host, a missing mandatory parameter, Get-Credential) — those are reported as 'awaiting_input', recovered by answering at the console or close_console. Targets the agent's active console directly — it does NOT route to a different console.

